                    {
                        "translation_id": "aaa23ff3-a53d-47d4-abdb-300bb83fa3eb",
                        "source_entry_id": "f8f6bfa1-6d8e-323f-9e48-051a8c1c2c46",
                        "source_sense_id": "48ebc5af-88d0-3ad2-af2a-30fd9d9cbad1",
                        "source_sense_description": "een snaarinstrument dat voornamelijk gebruikt wordt in het Duitstalige deel van Europa",
                        "target_lang_word": "cittern",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cittern",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a0d0ece-7a1a-3498-80c3-687498fb2266",
                                        "entry_id": "fcc50f90-2d77-3e3f-9b4f-36fc667c0358",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stringed instrument (chordophone), played with a plectrum (a pick), and most commonly possessing four wire strings and chromatic frets, which is a precursor to the modern day guitar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e6e00d4-0f46-4f0b-8efa-c7a93d813f04",
                                                "sense_id": "8a0d0ece-7a1a-3498-80c3-687498fb2266",
                                                "text": "This discourse took us much time, till it was time to go to bed; but we being merry, we bade my Lady goodnight, and intended to have gone to the Post-house to drink, and hear a pretty girl play of the cittern (and indeed we should have lain there, but by a mistake we did not), but it was late, and we could not hear her, and the guard came to examine what we were; so we returned to our Inn and to bed, the page and I in one bed, and the two captains in another, all in one chamber, where we had very good mirth with our most abominable lodging."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91146f88-d6e7-4829-8a93-4932dae89dc5",
                                                "sense_id": "8a0d0ece-7a1a-3498-80c3-687498fb2266",
                                                "text": "1911, Cittern, article in Encyclopædia Britannica Eleventh Edition,\nThe cittern consisted of a pear-shaped body similar to that of the lute but with a flat back and sound-board joined by ribs. The neck was provided with a fretted fingerboard; the head was curved and surmounted by a grotesque head of a woman or of an animal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d52646b3-3317-4aca-bbbd-d623cf1aaf6d",
                                                "sense_id": "8a0d0ece-7a1a-3498-80c3-687498fb2266",
                                                "text": "The advent of the Spanish guitar in England led to the wane in the popularity of the cittern, also known at that time in contradistinction as the English or wire-strung guitar, although the two instruments differed in many particulars."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46251e20-da25-4224-9f04-164c6bec4ae4",
                                                "sense_id": "8a0d0ece-7a1a-3498-80c3-687498fb2266",
                                                "text": "Antwerp was world-famous for its harpsichords, but it was also a centre, in the 16th century, where citterns, lutes, viols and later violins were constructed with skill."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d183eb35-5ad4-409b-8449-59788aee0769",
                        "source_entry_id": "f8f6bfa1-6d8e-323f-9e48-051a8c1c2c46",
                        "source_sense_id": "48ebc5af-88d0-3ad2-af2a-30fd9d9cbad1",
